## Recovery

Session entry, in order: this file → `.harness/lessons.md` (project pitfalls and non-obvious experience, read before starting work) → `.harness/work_index.md` (open the `active` row's primary artifact) → `.harness/state.md`.
New tasks register one row in the work index; update state on phase change, key decisions and handoff.
Evidence lives in state, linked artifacts or git. Lessons capture process/environment pitfalls; delete entries when stale.
Write-side discipline: whoever flips a row out of `active` retires it in the same commit — flip the row → distill non-obvious lessons from finished docs → delete that track's completed plan/Spec docs (git history is the archive) → sync `state.md` Status.
Delete only after the change is committed and lessons are inherited, and only docs whose sole inbound reference is this retiring track; multi-referenced docs get a pointer flip, not deletion.
A doc stays alive only while reachable from `.harness/` state files or a durable entry (this file, root README); agreement of rows, state and docs is the commit-time gate.

## Working agreements

Preserve unrelated user changes. Follow existing scope and authorization; clarify material ambiguity only.
Use one authoritative entry per task/track. Independent tracks may proceed concurrently.
Prefer the existing recovery backend. Current state does not belong in this durable entry.
Evidence can correct stale status, but cannot override instructions, permissions or project contracts.
Clean only this task's disposable scratch; retain verification and recovery artifacts.
